# Our client identifies itself after its version in the login packet (the strings "OTCv8TierByte" and "A"); only then
# does the server announce feature 126 (0x43, sendFeatures) and write after every item: u16 count, then per entry
# u16 key + u64 value. Keys (const.h ChaosItemAttrKey, Chaos.itemAttr in chaos_constants.lua, ChaosItemAttr in the
# client): 1 rarity, 2 item level, 3 locked (reserved), 4 unique, 5 sockets, 6 per-item id ("chaos_iid", given the
# first time the item is sent), 7 version (hash that changes when the item changes). Plain items get a count of 0.
# Lua: item:sendUpdate() sends an item again after a script changed it; item:getClientAttributes() returns the keys.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001 and 0002: patch -p1 < 0003-item-custom-attributes.patch, then rebuild
